onical. The subscript Q₁ → \"q1\" (minimum flow rate). I'll use attribute \"q1\", \"q2\", \"q3\", \"q4\", and ratio \"q3_q1_ratio\". Units m³/h (unit_symbol \"m³/h\").\n\nNow, for matrix_tables rows, each row object: {\"nominal_diameter\": 20, \"q1\": 0.004, \"q2\": 0.006, \"q3\": 2.5, \"q4\": 3.125, \"q3_q1_ratio\": 630}.\n\nLet me also decide table names: \"Flow rates – sonico NANO DN 20\", etc. Description could note page. Keep simple.\n\nAlso — page info: \"Page 7 of 10 pages\" appears; Verze 20-001 (version of form). Not needed in JSON. page_total: 10 could go into certificate: \"page_total\": 10. That's present. I'll include it. project_number? Not present. member_state: CZ is implied by certificate number suffix \"CZ1\" and the ČMI seal; the stamp says \"Český metrologický institut\". member_state \"CZ\"? It's derivable. I might include oiml_issuer_id? Not present explicitly. I'll keep certificate minimal: number, scheme, page_total. Maybe member_state \"CZ\" — the stamp is in Czech; issuing authority is Czech Metrology Institute. I'll include member_state: \"CZ\". Hmm, it's an inference but a safe one. I'll include it.\n\nissuing_authority: The stamp mentions \"Český metrologický institut\". Name only. Include? The stamp is present in fragment. I'll include issuing_authority: {name: \"Český metrologický institut\"} — reasonable. Address not in fragment.\n\nActually wait — should I be more conservative and omit issuing_authority since it's only a stamp description? The stamp clearly identifies the issuer (ČMI, which issued R49/2013-A-CZ1). I'll include name only.\n\nNow, characteristics.type_level: none applicable (fragment has no whole-cert attributes).\n\ncomponents: none.\n\ntest_reports: none.\n\nfootnotes: none.\n\nLet me now double-check mapping of Q₃/Q₁ colspan for DN20 table: The Q1 row had 4 cells; Q3/Q1 row: colspan=2 \"630\", \"800\", \"1000\". So col1-2 → 630, col3 → 800, col4 → 1000. Yes.\n\nBut check ratios: col1: 2.5/0.004=625→630 ✓; col2: 4/0.006=667→630? Hmm 4/0.006=666.7. Nominal 630 gives Q1=4/630=0.00635→0.006 ✓. OK, consistent with rounding to displayed precision. col3: 4/0.005=800 ✓. col4: 4/0.004=1000 ✓.\n\nWait, actually col2 Q1=0.006 gives 667 which rounds to 630? 666.7 → nominal R630 (closest standard is 630). Yes fine.\n\nHmm, actually wait: is it possible the mapping is different — e.g., colspan=2 covers columns... The Q1 row has 4 data cells after the label cell. The ratio row has label + colspan2 + 2 cells = covers 4 columns. Yes as I did.\n\nNow Q4/Q3 = 1.25 in all cases: 2.5→3.125 ✓, 4→5 ✓, 6.3→7.875 ✓, 10→12.5 ✓. Good.\n\nNow build JSON. Given the size, I'll be careful with commas.\n\nStructure:\n\n{\n  \"certificate\": {\n    \"number\": \"R49/2013-A-CZ1-24.02\",\n    \"scheme\": \"A\",\n    \"page_total\": 10,\n    \"member_state\": \"CZ\"\n  },\n  \"issuing_authority\": {\n    \"name\": \"Český metrologický institut\"\n  },\n  \"manufacturers\": [\n    {\"name\": \"GWF AG\"}\n  ],\n  \"certified_type\": {\n    \"category\": \"Water meter\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"sonico NANO\"]\n  },\n  \"model_family\": {\n    \"family_name\": \"sonico NANO\",\n    \"models\": [ ... 46 models ... ]\n  },\n  \"matrix_tables\": [ ...5 tables... ],\n  \"characteristics\": {\n    \"model_level\": [ 6 attribute entries ]\n  },\n  \"recommendation\": {\n    \"id\": \"R49\",\n    \"edition\": 2013,\n    \"scheme\": \"A\"\n  },\n  \"revision_history\": [\n    {\"revision\": \"3\"}\n  ]\n}\n\nHmm, revision_history entry with only revision — schema wants date and changes. I'll include just revision since that's all that's present. Or omit entirely. I'll include it minimal; it's truthful.\n\nActually, wait: should recommendation accuracy_classes be included? Not in fragment. Omit.\n\nmodels entries: {\"model_id\": \"DN20-Q3=2.5-R630\"}. Should I add attributes like nominal_diameter? To keep JSON smaller, model_id encodes it, and matrix_tables + model_level carry the values. I'll add attributes with nomi